CHAPTER.VERS:
In the fourteenth day of this month, at evening, you

          {+}
         will keep it in its appointed season: according to all the statutes of it, and according to all its ordinances, you

          {+}
         will keep it.

And Moses said to them, Wait

          {+}
        , that I may hear what Yahweh will command concerning you

          {+}
        .

Speak to the sons of Israel, saying, If any man of you

          {+}
         or of your

          {+}
         generations will be unclean by reason of a dead body, or be on a journey far off, yet he will keep the Passover to Yahweh.

And if a stranger will sojourn among you

          {+}
        , and will keep the Passover to Yahweh; according to the statute of the Passover, and according to its ordinance, so he will do: you

          {+}
         will have one statute, both for the sojourner, and for him who is born in the land.
